            {
              "$type": "Models.Core.Folder, Models",
              "ShowInDocs": false,
              "GraphsPerPage": 6,
              "Name": "SAE",
              "ResourceName": null,
              "Children": [
                {
                  "$type": "Models.Factorial.Experiment, Models",
                  "DisabledSimNames": null,
                  "Name": "SAE_Oats_2020",
                  "ResourceName": null,
                  "Children": [
                    {
                      "$type": "Models.Memo, Models",
                      "Text": "*\tThe aim of this SAE funded project is to assess contrasting plant traits in oats.\r\n\r\n*\tThe focus is on early-vigour as a critical plant trait in winter-sown oat catch crops. \r\n\r\n*\tEarly vigour influences N uptake rate by the catch crop and by association may also reduce the amount of residual soil N at risk of leaching. \r\n\r\n*\tThe treatments are 6 oat genotypes with potential differences for early canopy expansion.\r\n\r\n*\tThe experiment had 4 replicates\r\n\r\n*\t400 kg N/ha at sowing to mimic  aurine patch to ne mopped by the oat catch crop\r\n\r\n*\tKey differences in early vigour were due to individual leaf size in first 6 leaves\r\n\r\n",
                      "Name": "Experiment Description",
                      "ResourceName": null,
                      "Children": [],
                      "Enabled": true,
                      "ReadOnly": false
                    },
