                                      "Text": "# Comparing cultivars Coronet and PFR 100-05\n\n- Data collected by **Mike George**\n- Data sits in: https://iplant.plantandfood.co.nz/project/I161208\n\n## Context: \n- PFR 100-05 showed faster canopy cloure rates via drone aerial photos\n- Field trial was done to identify mechanisms. \n\n##Main differences between cultivars were:\n\n- Larger leaves by PRR 100-05 (45-80% larger)\n- Taller stems by PFR 100-05 (50% taller)\n\n## Observations\n\n- We agreed to keep only leaf size as genotype difference. Height also differed as:\n- [Structure].HeightModel.PotentialHeight.XYPairs.Y = 13,204,820,820\n- [Structure].HeightModel.PotentialHeight.XYPairs.Y = 20,300,1200,1200",
                                      "Name": "ReadMe",
                                      "ResourceName": null,
                                      "Children": [],
                                      "Enabled": true,
                                      "ReadOnly": false
                                    }
                                  ],
                                  "Enabled": true,
                                  "ReadOnly": false
                                }
                              ],
                              "Enabled": true,
                              "ReadOnly": false
                            },
                            {
                              "$type": "Models.Report, Models",
                              "VariableNames": [
                                "[Clock].Today as ReportDate",
                                "[Clock].Today.Year as Year",
                                "",
                                "[FactorLabels].Script.AGENT_NO as AGENT_NO",
                                "[FactorLabels].Script.Lat as Lat",
                                "[FactorLabels].Script.Lon as Lon",
                                "[FactorLabels].Script.GCM as GCM",
                                "[FactorLabels].Script.RCP as RCP",
                                "[FactorLabels].Script.TS as TimeSlice",
                                "[FactorLabels].Script.SoilStamp as SoilStamp",
                                "[CropManagement].Script.CurrentCrop as CropSpecies",
                                "",
                                "sum([Soil].Water.MM) as SoilWater_Total",
                                "sum([Soil].Urea.kgha) as SoilUrea_Total",
                                "sum([Soil].NH4.kgha) as SoilNH4_Total",
                                "sum([Soil].NO3.kgha) as SoilNO3_Total",
                                "(sum([Soil].Urea.kgha) + sum([Soil].NH4.kgha) + sum([Soil].NO3.kgha)) as SoilMineralN_Total",
                                "[CropManagement].Script.HarvestedWt as HarvestedCropBiomass",
                                "[CropManagement].Script.HarvestedN as HarvestedCropN",
                                "[CropManagement].Script.HarvestedNconc as HarvestedCropNconc",
                                "[CropManagement].Script.CropYield as CropYield",
                                "",
                                "[CropManagement].Script.SowDOY as SowingDOY",
                                "[CropManagement].Script.HarvestDOY as HarvestingDOY",
                                "[CropManagement].Script.CoverCropCultivar as CoverCropCultivar",
                                "[Oats].Panicle.HeadNumber",
                                "",
                                "[ExtraVariables].Script.CropAboveGroundBiomassN as UptakeN_Cum",
                                "[ExtraVariables].Script.AccumSoilOMMineralisedToLayer as SoilOMMineralisedNToGivenLayer_Cum",
                                "([ExtraVariables].Script.AccumSoilOMMineralisedToLayer+[ExtraVariables].Script.AccumSurfaceOMMineralisation) as MineralisedNToGivenLayer_Cum",
                                "[ExtraVariables].Script.AccumDenitrifiedNToLayer as DenitrifiedNToGivenLayer_Cum",
                                "[ExtraVariables].Script.AccumFlowNAtLayer as LeachedNAtGivenLayer_Cum",
                                "[ExtraVariables].Script.SumUreaToLayer as UreaToGivenLayer_Sum",
                                "[ExtraVariables].Script.SumNH4ToLayer as NH4ToGivenLayer_Sum",
                                "[ExtraVariables].Script.SumNO3ToLayer as NO3ToGivenLayer_Sum",
                                "[ExtraVariables].Script.SumMineralNToLayer as MineralNToGivenLayer_Sum",
                                "[ExtraVariables].Script.SumFOMNToLayer as FOMNToGivenLayer_Sum",
                                "[ExtraVariables].Script.SumMicrobialNToLayer as MicrobialNToGivenLayer_Sum",
                                "[ExtraVariables].Script.SumHumicNToLayer as HumicNToGivenLayer_Sum",
                                "[ExtraVariables].Script.SumOrganicNToLayer as OrganicNToGivenLayer_Sum",
                                "[ExtraVariables].Script.SumOrganicCToLayer as OrganicCToGivenLayer_Sum",
                                "[Soil].SoilNitrogen.oc[1] as OC_TopLayer",
                                "[ExtraVariables].Script.DeltaSoilMineralNToLayer as SoilMineralN_DeltaToGivenLayer",
                                "[ExtraVariables].Script.DeltaSoilOrganicNToLayer as SoilOrganicN_DeltaToGivenLayer",
                                "",
                                "[ExtraVariables].Script.CropAboveGroundBiomassWt as CropBiomass_Cum",
                                "[ExtraVariables].Script.CropAboveGroundBiomassN as CropN_Cum",
                                "[ExtraVariables].Script.CropAboveGroundBiomassNConc as CropNconc"
                              ],
                              "EventNames": [
                                ""
                              ],
                              "GroupByVariableName": null,
                              "Name": "Output",
                              "ResourceName": null,
                              "Children": [
                                {
                                  "$type": "Models.Memo, Models",
                                  "Text": "Measurements \n\nSoil samples will be collected from each plot: \n\n0-15, 15-30 and 30-60 cm depths (or to stones). \n\nComposite sample of 10 cores 1 m apart following a 10 m transect across the plot. The intensive regime is to account for urine patch variability, and ensure we intercept a proportionally accurate number of urine patches across the plot. \n\nSoil mineral N (nitrate and ammonium) measured at every depth. \n\nBasic mineral analysis for 0-15 cm depth (combined sample from all reps). \n\nFollowing emergence, plant counts will be performed to assess achieved plant population \n\nCrop canopy development will be monitored at regular intervals using a hand-held Greenseeker (reflectance measurements). \n\nBiomass will be measured at three key crop stages of the ‘control treatment’ (all treatments simultaneously measured at each sampling occasion): \n\nGS21 (tillering), September \n\nGS32 (2nd node), October \n\nGS45 (booting) = final harvest, November \n\n \n\nFor each biomass harvest, 3x 0.5 m2 quadrats (1.5 m2 in total) in each plot will be cut at ground level and total fresh biomass weighed. A ≈300g subsample will be taken, weighed after drying at 60°C until constant weight (dry matter content), and then ground and analysed for total N content using a LECO CNS analyser in order to determine crop N uptake. \n\n \n\nAt final harvest, a separate subsample will also be taken and sent to Hills Laboratories to measure feed quality. \n\n \n\nClimate data (rainfall, air and soil temperature, radiation) will be recorded via a local NIWA or on-site weather station for each site. \n\n ",
                                  "Name": "Memo",
                                  "ResourceName": null,
                                  "Children": [],
                                  "Enabled": true,
                                  "ReadOnly": false
                                }
                              ],
                              "Enabled": true,
                              "ReadOnly": false
                            },
