            {
              "$type": "Models.Core.Folder, Models",
              "ShowInDocs": false,
              "GraphsPerPage": 6,
              "Name": "SLMACC",
              "ResourceName": null,
              "Children": [
                {
                  "$type": "Models.Factorial.Experiment, Models",
                  "DisabledSimNames": [],
                  "Name": "SLMACC_Canterbury_2020",
                  "ResourceName": null,
                  "Children": [
                    {
                      "$type": "Models.Memo, Models",
                      "Text": "* \tTrial location: Springston, Canterbury\n*\tCoordinates: 43.641°S, 172.349°E\n*\tSoil: Balmoral\n*\tWeather station: Broadfield\n*\tThis experiment evaluated oat populations (i.e. target of 0 [fallow],150, 300, 450 plants/m2) \n*\tTwo row spacings (75 & 150 cm) were also evaluated in the trial (see factors)\n*\tNote that these ppopulations were not achieved so, actual plant counts are used in the model (see factors).\n* \tThe paddock was previously in a kale crop\n*\tThis is a grazed field and grazing occured on the winter (kale) crop prior to sowing oats\n*\tIrrigation: a total of 210 mm was applied to all treatments (source: BM. SM)\n\n*\tAccording to the DairyNZ fact sheet (https://www.dairynz.co.nz/media/253803/1-74_Kale_growing_a_high_yielding_crop.pdf), Kale yield can vary (12-17 t DM)depending on the variety (short, intermediate & giant). Utilisation efficiency is 80-85%.\n*\tAccording to Chakwizira et al 2015(https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/epdf/10.1080/00288233.2015.1016538?needAccess=true&role=button), a well fertilised crop contains ~1.3%.\n*\tBased on a 15 t DM/ha (average yield), aboveground residue will be 2.25 t DM/ha. \n* \tRoot biomass is assumed to be 9.9 % (i.e. 1.485 t DM/ha) according to Urlic et al 2015(https://www.researchgate.net/publication/273506706_Phosphorus-Use_Efficiency_of_Kale_Genotypes_from_Coastal_Croatia/figures?lo=1).\n*\tWe can approximate that Root N conc is ~1.3% based on Canola research data",
                      "Name": "Experiment Description",
                      "ResourceName": null,
                      "Children": [],
                      "Enabled": true,
                      "ReadOnly": false
                    },
